# Task

## Captain's words
Trang About phải hiện số phiên bản của app.

## What we already know
- The site is built with Hugo; `make build` writes it to public/ (PROJECT.md, "How to work here").
- The version is the one line in VERSION at the repository root (report of scout k1, section 2).
- Unknown: whether the About page is a layout template or a content file.

## Build
- Show the text of VERSION on the About page, as "Version <text>".
- Out of scope: other pages, the footer, how VERSION is written.

## Acceptance
- The built About page contains "Version " followed by the text of VERSION. verify: `make build && grep -o 'Version [^<]*' public/about/index.html`
- The site still builds. verify: `make build`; quote its last lines.

## Open decisions
none

# How to read the task
`## Captain's words` is what the captain actually said about this task, word for word; it is the contract, and where any other section disagrees with it, it wins.
The other sections are the Mate's specification of it: what is already known, what to build, how each result is checked, and which choices are not yours.
The Mate never reads this repository, so what `## What we already know` says about it is second-hand; check it against what you find, and say where it was wrong.
Do only what `## Build` asks for.
Anything under its `Out of scope:` line stays out, and a generalization, consistency sweep, or extra hardening the task did not ask for is follow-up work to mention when you hand back, not scope to add.
`## Open decisions` lists choices that are not yours to make.
When you reach one of these, append `needs-decision:` naming it, and stop.
Do not pick an option, even the obvious one.

# Setup
You are in a disposable git worktree of `/ws/shop`, on branch `mate/k3`, branched from `main`.

Verify isolation before anything else.
Run `pwd -P` and `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`; both must resolve to `/ws/.worktrees/shop-k3`, not the project's primary checkout at `/ws/shop`.
If the top-level path is the primary checkout, STOP: do not edit or commit here, append `needs-decision: launched in primary checkout, not an isolated worktree` to the status file, and stop.

# Rules
1. Push only your own branch `mate/k3`, to `origin`, and open a pull request for it against `main` with `gh pr create`. Never push any other branch, never force-push, and never merge the pull request.
2. Stay inside this worktree; modify nothing outside it except the two files this brief names by absolute path: the status file and `/ws/.mate/projects/shop/crews/k3/handback.md`.
3. Report status by appending one line:
   `echo "{state}: {one short line}" >> $MATE_STATUS`
   You have exactly three states, and no others: `working`, `needs-decision`, `wait-mate`.
   - `working: {phase}` - you are making progress.
   - `needs-decision: {summary of the options}` - you cannot decide this yourself. Stop your turn; somebody will type an answer into this pane and you carry on.
   - `wait-mate: {one line}` - you have done all you can and are handing the task back to the Mate. It is your last line.
   - `pr-open: {url}` - the form of `wait-mate` for a pull request you opened; the Definition of done says when. It is your last line.
   Never write `blocked`, `failed`, `finished` or `done`. Those words belong to the app and to the Mate: `blocked` is what the app calls a crew that cannot speak at all, and whether the task finished or failed is the Mate's decision, not yours.
   Append `working: {what you are about to do}` once, as your very first action, before you read or change anything. Until you do, nobody can tell a Crew that started work from one whose harness never came up.
   After that first line, report sparingly: each append wakes the Mate, so write only phase changes a supervisor would act on, plus `needs-decision` and `wait-mate`. No step-by-step FYI progress lines.
4. If you hit the same obstacle twice, append `needs-decision: {why, and what you would try next}` and stop; the Mate will help. A missing key, a missing permission, two plausible directions - all of these are `needs-decision`, because you can still ask.
5. If a decision belongs to a human - a product choice, a destructive action, anything under `## Open decisions`, or anything else the task left open that the repository does not settle for you - append `needs-decision: {summary of the options}` and stop. The Mate will reply with the decision.
   Do not settle it by taking whichever option looks most natural and mentioning it afterwards. Once you have shipped a guess it is indistinguishable from an instruction you were given, and the only moment anyone could have corrected it has passed.
6. If you genuinely cannot finish the task, that is not a failure you declare: append `wait-mate: could not do X because Y` and stop. The Mate decides what happens next.
7. If the captain adds to the task while you work, the app appends their words to `## Captain's words` in `/ws/.mate/projects/shop/crews/k3/brief.md` and sends you one line saying so; read that section again and carry on with it.

