# Definition of done
This task is delivered through a GitHub pull request: no pipeline, and the pull request is merged by the Mate or on GitHub, never by you.
The task is complete only when it is committed on this branch, the hand-back below is written, and the branch is pushed with a pull request open.
Keep the branch a clean fast-forward onto `main`; if it has advanced, rebase onto it so the eventual merge stays a fast-forward.

# Before you hand back
Run every `verify:` under `## Acceptance` yourself, against the committed branch.
Where a `verify:` asks you to find the project's own check, find it, run it, and name the exact command you ran.
Then write `/ws/.mate/projects/shop/crews/k3/handback.md`.
It is outside this worktree on purpose, like the status file: the worktree is removed when the task is closed, and that file is kept.
It has exactly these three parts:

```markdown
| criterion | pass/fail | command | output |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| (one row per line of ## Acceptance, in order) | pass or fail | the exact command you ran | the few lines of its output that prove the result |

## Deviations from Build
Everything you did that ## Build did not ask for, or did differently, and why; or none.

## Still open
What you could not settle, follow-up work you noticed but did not do, and anything ## What we already know got wrong; or none.
```

A criterion that fails is reported as `fail` with its output, never left out or softened.
When the work is committed and the hand-back is written, deliver it:
1. `git push -u origin mate/k3`.
2. `gh pr create --base main --head mate/k3 --title "<one line>" --body-file /ws/.mate/projects/shop/crews/k3/handback.md`.
3. `echo "pr-open: <the pull request URL gh printed>" >> $MATE_STATUS`.
4. `/usr/local/bin/mate pr watch shop k3 <the same URL>`. It returns at once and keeps watching in the background; it wakes the Mate when the pull request is merged or closed. Run it once.

Then stop. `pr-open:` is your hand-back line for this task, in place of `wait-mate: ready in branch mate/k3`.
You stay alive after it: the Mate may send you review comments or a failing check. Fix them on this branch and push; the pull request follows the branch. Never open a second one.
If you could not finish, write the hand-back anyway, push nothing, and append `wait-mate: could not do X because Y`.
The Mate has your hand-back and branch diff reviewed against `## Captain's words` and `## Acceptance`; once the review passes, the pull request is merged.

Do NOT merge the pull request. Do NOT push any branch but `mate/k3`. Do NOT force-push.

